      "content": "makes sense. i was thinking more specifically about the demographic shifts. like, in some of the older districts, we're seeing a lot more diversity coming in and the racial makeup is changing fast. from an investment standpoint, does that usually signal a \"refining\" of the area that brings value, or does it tend to lead to instability and lower property values in the long run? i want to know if i should be looking for high-homogeneity areas or if the diversifying ones are actually better bets.",
